message.content:
{
  "generated_description": "The 20th Livestock Census provides detailed statistics on livestock and related assets, covering cattle, buffalo, sheep, goat, horse, pony, mule, donkey, camel and pig across rural and urban areas. It also captures information on livestock rearing, including poultry and the implements and machinery used for livestock rearing. Published by the Department of Animal Husbandry and Dairying and the Ministry of Fisheries, Animal Husbandry and Dairying, the census supports planning and monitoring of animal husbandry activities in India at state and district level.",
  "generated_sector": "Agriculture; Animal Husbandry"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The 6th Minor Irrigation Census provides village-level schedules and scheme details for minor irrigation across 33 States/UTs, covering both ground water schemes and surface water schemes. It supports assessment of minor irrigation infrastructure and planning by documenting relevant census schedules and related documentation for the reference year 2017-18. Published by the Department of Water Resources, River Development & Ganga Rejuvenation, the collection is useful for researchers, planners, and administrators working on irrigation development and water resource management.",
  "generated_sector": "Water Resources; Drinking Water"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The 7th Minor Irrigation Census - Village Schedule, Ground Water Schemes, Surface Water Schemes compiles village-level information on minor irrigation systems across India, covering both ground water schemes and surface water schemes. It supports assessment of irrigation infrastructure and planning by providing structured schedules and related census documentation for the reference year 2023-24. Published by the Ministry of Jal Shakti; Department of Water Resources, River Development & Ganga Rejuvenation, it is useful for researchers, planners, and administrators working on water resources and irrigation development.",
  "generated_sector": "Water Resources; Drinking Water"
}

{
  "generated_description": "ARPU (Average Revenue Per User) - CDMA provides telecom revenue performance indicators for India, covering circle-wise and metro details. It supports analysis of postpaid, prepaid and blended ARPU trends to compare monetization across service areas and urban markets. Published by NITI Aayog, the catalog is useful for telecom planning, benchmarking operator performance, and informing policy discussions on consumer revenue outcomes in CDMA networks.",
  "generated_sector": "Information and Communications; Telecom"
}

{
  "generated_description": "ARPU (Average Revenue per User) data provides telecom revenue and usage insights for India, covering circle-wise reporting as well as metro and operator categories such as BSNL/MTNL and all private service providers. It supports analysis of postpaid, prepaid and blended ARPU, helping compare monetization performance across service provider types and geographic circles. Published by NITI Aayog, the catalog is useful for telecom market monitoring, benchmarking, and policy and planning focused on user revenue trends.",
  "generated_sector": "Information and Communications; Telecom"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog provides gender- and age-band wise counts of Aadhaar generated and of enrolment applications rejected, based on the latest updated date available in the underlying CSV files. It supports monitoring of Aadhaar enrolment trends and rejection patterns across India, enabling analysis for policy review and service delivery improvements. Data are published by NITI Aayog and the Unique Identification Authority of India (UIDAI) and are useful for demographic insights into Aadhaar uptake and enrolment friction.",
  "generated_sector": "Governance and Administration; Union/State Government Administration"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog provides service provider wise gross revenue data for telecom access services in India. It supports analysis of revenue generation by individual providers, enabling comparisons across operators and insights for policy planning and market monitoring. Published by NITI Aayog, the collection is useful for researchers, regulators, and analysts tracking telecom sector performance and financial trends at the provider level.",
  "generated_sector": "Information and Communications; Telecom"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog focuses on access to household amenities—especially toilet facilities—along with tap water, radio, television, and telephone, in rural India. It highlights conditions in worst performing states in terms of toilet facilities, using 2011 as the reference year. The insights support planning and monitoring of sanitation and related household service improvements by NITI Aayog, with a state-wise perspective across the listed states.",
  "generated_sector": "Rural; Development"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog covers accessibility and availability of schools in urban slum areas, based on a sample survey capturing students’ responses on how far schools are and how schools are managed. It presents indicators on school distance and availability by management type such as government, government-aided, local body and private. The findings support evaluation of Sarva Shiksha Abhiyan, 2010, using survey work undertaken by Programme Evaluation Organisation (PEO), Planning Commission. The coverage is for India.",
  "generated_sector": "Education; Elementary"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog covers sample survey findings on the accessibility of banking facilities before and after completion of rural roads under the scheme. It captures beneficiary responses on changes in access to banking services linked to rural road improvements, supporting evaluation of economic and social service delivery outcomes. The evidence is based on a survey conducted by the Programme Evaluation Organisation (PEO), Planning Commission, covering India. The study spans multiple rural roads, habitations, blocks and districts, enabling assessment at the beneficiary level.",
  "generated_sector": "Infrastructure; Roads"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog covers sample-survey findings on the accessibility of bus stands and railway stations before and after completion of rural roads under the scheme. It captures beneficiary responses on changes in access to economic and social services across selected rural locations, based on a Programme Evaluation Organisation (PEO) study. Published by NITI Aayog, the data supports evaluation of rural road impacts on connectivity and service access in India.",
  "generated_sector": "Infrastructure; Roads"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog covers sample survey findings on the accessibility of educational institutions before and after completion of rural roads under the Scheme. It captures beneficiary responses on how improved rural road connectivity affected access to education across selected rural locations in India. The evidence is based on a survey undertaken by the Programme Evaluation Organisation (PEO), Planning Commission, supporting evaluation and planning for rural infrastructure and social service outcomes. Published under NITI Aayog, it is useful for impact assessment and policy monitoring.",
  "generated_sector": "Infrastructure; Roads"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog covers sample survey findings on the accessibility of health care centers/hospitals before and after completion of rural roads under the scheme. It captures beneficiary responses on changes in access to hospitals and related economic and social services across sampled rural locations. The data is based on a survey undertaken by the Programme Evaluation Organisation (PEO), Planning Commission, supporting evaluation of rural road impacts on health service accessibility. Coverage is for India.",
  "generated_sector": "Infrastructure; Roads"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog covers sample survey findings on the accessibility of markets and town/urban centers before and after completion of rural roads under the scheme. It captures beneficiary responses on changes in access to economic and social services linked to markets and urban centers across a selected set of rural road interventions. Published by NITI Aayog, the evidence supports evaluation of rural road outcomes and planning for improved connectivity in India.",
  "generated_sector": "Infrastructure; Roads"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog covers sample survey findings on the accessibility of post offices before and after completion of rural roads under the scheme. It captures beneficiary responses on how access to economic and social services changes following road completion, supporting evaluation of rural infrastructure outcomes. The data is based on a survey conducted by Programme Evaluation Organisation (PEO), Planning Commission, spanning 14 districts, 27 blocks, 138 roads, 138 habitations, and 1380 beneficiary households. Coverage is for India.",
  "generated_sector": "Infrastructure; Roads"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog covers sample survey findings on accessibility to upper primary education in India, focusing on school age and recent openings, and on slum areas lacking upper primary schools. It is based on an evaluation study undertaken by the Programme Evaluation Organisation (PEO), Planning Commission for the “Evaluation Report On Sarva Shiksha Abhiyan, 2010”, with a reference period of 2003 to 2007. The insights support planning and monitoring of elementary education access and infrastructure needs under Sarva Shiksha Abhiyan.",
  "generated_sector": "Education; Elementary"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog focuses on accident-related information for Ujjain, Madhya Pradesh, supporting analysis of urban safety and incident patterns within the city. It is aligned with the Smart Cities Mission under the Ministry of Housing and Urban Affairs, enabling stakeholders to review accident occurrences and use the insights for planning, monitoring, and mitigation efforts. The scope is city-level for Ujjain, Madhya Pradesh, with resources organized around the theme of “Accident : Ujjain.”",
  "generated_sector": "Governance and Administration; Local Government Administration"
}

{
  "generated_description": "Accidental Deaths & Suicides in India (ADSI) compiles police-recorded information on natural and unnatural accidents, traffic accidents, and suicides. It tracks major causes such as traffic accidents, drowning, lightning, heart attacks, accidental fire, falls, and poisoning, alongside suicide causes including family problems, illness, and bankruptcy or indebtedness. The catalog provides all-India level incidence with age and gender-wise distribution and percentage variation, supporting analysis of trends in deaths and injuries over 1967 to 2023. Published by the Ministry of Home Affairs and the National Crime Records Bureau (NCRB).",
  "generated_sector": "Home Affairs and Enforcement; Police"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog covers category-wise accretion of coal reserves at the end of each year, supporting analysis of how coal reserve stocks change over time for the power sector. It provides data for 2005 to 2011, enabling trend assessment and planning for fuel availability in electricity generation. Published under NITI Aayog, the focus is on coal reserve dynamics in India, with indicators that support both indicated and inferred reserve perspectives.",
  "generated_sector": "Power and Energy; Non Renewable"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog brings together information on achievement on National Highways (NHs) in India, focusing on progress and performance related to road and highway development. It is intended to support monitoring and review of national highway initiatives and outcomes for planning, policy assessment, and infrastructure decision-making. Published under NITI Aayog, the resources help users understand how achievements on NHs evolve over time at the national level.",
  "generated_sector": "Infrastructure; Roads"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog brings together achievements data for the Family Welfare Programme, covering India-wide results from 2000 to 2012 and state-wise achievements for 2010-12. It focuses on reported numbers and rates that reflect programme performance across key family welfare indicators. The compilation supports monitoring, evaluation, and policy review by enabling comparisons over time and across states within the specified period. It is published by the Ministry of Statistics and Programme Implementation.",
  "generated_sector": "Health and Family welfare; Health"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog brings together achievements data from India’s Immunization Programme, covering key vaccines and maternal and child immunization outcomes such as BCG, DPT, Polio, Measles, and Tetanus. It spans 2000 to 2011 for all-India achievements and includes state-wise achievements for 2010-12. The information supports monitoring programme performance, identifying coverage gaps, and informing planning and evaluation for public health interventions. Published under the Ministry of Statistics and Programme Implementation.",
  "generated_sector": "Health and Family welfare; Health"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog brings together components-wise achievements of National Highways Development Projects (NHDP) for India, covering 2007-08 to 2011-12. It tracks NHDP component total length, the length completed for 4/6 lanes, and the length under implementation, along with contract counts and remaining balance for award of civil works. Published by the Ministry of Statistics and Programme Implementation, the collection supports monitoring of highway project progress and planning for road infrastructure delivery.",
  "generated_sector": "Transport; Road Transport"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog covers sample-survey findings on the activities of VECs (Village Education Committees), expressed as the share of VECs undertaking key functions. It focuses on monitoring and supervision, teacher-related processes, school infrastructure improvements, record-keeping for enrolled children, and efforts to improve enrolment and reduce out-of-school children. The evidence is drawn from an evaluation survey conducted by the Programme Evaluation Organisation (PEO) under NITI Aayog for Sarva Shiksha Abhiyan, 2010, across India.",
  "generated_sector": "Education; Elementary"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog brings together information on the actual change in forest cover across States/UTs in India, drawing on forest assessment reporting such as ISFR. It supports analysis of trends in forest cover over time for policy planning, monitoring, and evaluation of forestry and environmental interventions. Published under NITI Aayog, the resources are useful for researchers, government analysts, and stakeholders tracking changes in forest extent at the State/UT level.",
  "generated_sector": "Environment and Forest; Forest Resources"
}

{
  "generated_description": "Admin Boundaries provides access to administrative boundary layers for India, covering State, District, and Block boundaries. It supports mapping and spatial analysis for water-related planning and decision-making by enabling consistent geographies across datasets. The catalog is published by the Department of Water Resources, River Development & Ganga Rejuvenation, Ministry of Jal Shakti, and the National Water Informatics Centre, and is useful for applications that require standardized administrative units for groundwater and surface water studies.",
  "generated_sector": "Water Resources; Ground Water, Water Resources; Surface Water"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog provides administrative zone and ward mapping data for Pimpri Chinchwad, Maharashtra. It supports planning and governance use cases such as ward-level administration, boundary referencing, and spatial organization of local government jurisdictions. Published under the Ministry of Housing and Urban Affairs and the Smart Cities Mission, the resources focus on mapping structures used for municipal service delivery and administrative coordination within the city.",
  "generated_sector": "Governance and Administration; Local Government"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog brings together information on the Administration of Mineral Conservation and Development Rules 1988 and MCDR, 2017, focusing on compliance monitoring in India. It covers counts of mines inspected where violations are observed and subsequently rectified, including cases where operations are suspended. The scope also includes rule and sub-rule rectification following the issuance of show cause notices, supporting oversight and enforcement by the Ministry of Mines and the Indian Bureau of Mines.",
  "generated_sector": "Industries; Mining"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog covers the Administration of Mineral Conservation and Development Rules, 1988, focusing on regulatory provisions relevant to mineral conservation and development. It is intended to support compliance, enforcement, and reference use by stakeholders dealing with mine operations and related violations, including suspension-related aspects. Published under the Ministry of Mines through the Indian Bureau of Mines, the materials apply across India and are anchored to the 1988 rules framework.",
  "generated_sector": "Industries; Mining"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog brings together state-wise information on administrative units alongside rural health infrastructure, covering facilities such as DHs, CHCs, PHCs and Sub-Centres. It supports analysis of how governance structures align with primary healthcare capacity in rural areas. Published by the Ministry of Statistics and Programme Implementation, the resources are useful for planning, monitoring and compliance-oriented reviews of rural service delivery across India.",
  "generated_sector": "Health and Family welfare; Health"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog covers information on adolescent girls following health and hygiene care advice discussed during NHE, including practices related to cleanliness, monitoring, nutrition, self-confidence, and treatment of minor illnesses. It also captures themes such as age of marriage and the importance of education, alongside health and hygiene behaviors. Published by NITI Aayog, the resources provide India-wide coverage with state-wise details to support program planning and evaluation for adolescent health and related interventions.",
  "generated_sector": "Health and Family welfare; Health"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog covers information on adult cattle units dependent on forests in India. It supports analysis of forest-linked livestock dependence and can be used for planning, monitoring and policy discussions around sustainable forest use and livelihoods. Published under NITI Aayog, the catalog draws on forest-related reporting (including ISFR) to help stakeholders understand the scale of cattle units associated with forest dependence.",
  "generated_sector": "Environment and Forest; Forest Resources"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog provides all-India statistics on adult male cattle and buffalo and their use, covering categories such as breeding only, agriculture and breeding, and bullock cart and breeding. It supports analysis of livestock utilization patterns and planning for animal husbandry and related agricultural operations. Published by the Ministry of Statistics and Programme Implementation, the datasets are intended for researchers, policymakers, and program managers working on breeding and draft-animal use in India.",
  "generated_sector": "Agriculture; Animal Husbandry"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog focuses on advance pollutant and air quality monitoring for Agartala city in Tripura. It covers key air pollutant concentrations including PM2.5, PM10, NO2, SO2, and O3, supporting analysis of urban air quality trends and exposure-related planning. Published under the Ministry of Housing and Urban Affairs through the Smart Cities Mission, the resources are useful for city-level environmental assessment and targeted mitigation efforts.",
  "generated_sector": "Environment and Forest; Industrial Air Pollution"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog focuses on advance air pollutants in Kakinada city, Andhra Pradesh, covering key ambient pollutants such as PM2.5, PM2.10, CO, NO2, and O3. It supports monitoring of air quality indicators for the 2020-2021 period, useful for urban health risk assessment and local environmental management. Published under the Ministry of Housing and Urban Affairs through the Smart Cities Mission, the resources align with residential air pollution concerns in Kakinada.",
  "generated_sector": "Environment and Forest; Residential Air Pollution"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog covers advances extended by Public Sector Banks to agriculture and other priority sectors, including micro and small enterprises and self-help groups. It presents financial indicators such as Adjusted Net Bank Credit across multiple years, enabling analysis of credit trends and sectoral flow of bank financing. Published by the Ministry of Finance, Department of Economic Affairs, the collection supports monitoring of priority-sector lending and related economic planning for India.",
  "generated_sector": "Finance; Economy"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog focuses on the age of establishment for Kohima, capturing how long establishments have been operating in the city of Kohima, Nagaland. It supports analysis of business maturity and local economic development patterns, useful for urban planning, investment decisions, and Smart Cities Mission initiatives. Published under the Ministry of Housing and Urban Affairs with involvement from Smart Cities Mission, Nagaland and Kohima, the catalog helps stakeholders compare establishment longevity across the city’s ecosystem.",
  "generated_sector": "Governance and Administration; Union/State Government Administration"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog brings together Census 1991 data on age, sex, and educational level for India and States. It supports analysis of population distribution by gender and age-group across categories such as illiterate, literate without educational level, and multiple education levels including primary, middle, matriculation/secondary, and higher secondary. The Registrar General and Census Commissioner, India, under the Ministry of Home Affairs, enables demographic and education-focused planning and research using census-based population enumerations.",
  "generated_sector": "Census and Surveys; Census"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog brings together Census 1991 data on age, sex and level of education for India. It supports analysis of literacy and educational attainment across age groups, including categories such as illiterate and literate, and education levels from primary to graduate and postgraduate. The coverage also includes professional and technical qualifications (including engineering, medicine, agriculture and dairying degrees) and educational breakdowns for Scheduled Castes and Scheduled Tribes. Published by the Ministry of Home Affairs, Department of Home, and the Registrar General and Census Commissioner, India.",
  "generated_sector": "Census and Surveys; Census"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog brings together Census 1991 data on age, sex and marital status for India and States. It covers key population characteristics such as age-group distribution and marital categories including never married, married, widowed, divorced and separated, alongside Scheduled Castes and Scheduled Tribes population. These statistics support demographic analysis, social research and planning by enabling comparisons across age and marital status profiles. Published by the Ministry of Home Affairs, Department of Home, Registrar General and Census Commissioner, India.",
  "generated_sector": "Census and Surveys; Census"
}

{
  "generated_description": "Age-group-wise Victims of (Incest, Other and Total) Rape Cases presents rape victim counts for India, broken down by age groups and by type—incest, other, and total. The series supports analysis of how victimization varies across age bands and helps compare patterns between incest-related and non-incest rape cases. Published by the Ministry of Home Affairs, Department of States, and the National Crime Records Bureau (NCRB), it is useful for crime monitoring, policy planning, and targeted prevention efforts.",
  "generated_sector": "Home Affairs and Enforcement; Police"
}

{
  "generated_description": "Crime statistics on age-group-wise victims of kidnapping and abduction in India, covering reported cases and victim counts by purpose. Victims are classified by sex (male and female) and by age groups (0-10, 10-15, 15-18, 18-30, 30-50, and 50 & above). The catalog supports analysis of patterns in kidnapping and abduction, including purpose-wise victimization, for policing, research, and policy planning. Published by the Ministry of Home Affairs and the National Crime Records Bureau (NCRB).",
  "generated_sector": "Home Affairs and Enforcement; Police"
}

{
  "generated_description": "Crime statistics on age-group-wise victims of murder in India, covering total cases reported and the number of murder victims by gender. Victim age is classified into 0-10, 10-15, 15-18, 18-30, 30-50, and 50 and above, enabling analysis of how victimization varies across age bands. The data supports research, policy planning, and monitoring of trends in violent crime. It is published by the Ministry of Home Affairs, Department of States, through the National Crime Records Bureau (NCRB).",
  "generated_sector": "Home Affairs and Enforcement; Police"
}

{
  "generated_description": "Agency-wise records of extramural Research and Development (R&D) projects approved in India, covering the number of projects and their approved cost. The catalog supports analysis of research funding and project distribution across sponsoring agencies, helping track scientific investment patterns and inform policy and planning. It is published by the Ministry of Science and Technology and the Department of Science and Technology (DST) through the National Science and Technology Management Information System (NSTMIS).",
  "generated_sector": "Science and Technology; Research & Development"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog brings together state-wise and category-wise information on aggregate technical and commercial losses of State Power Utilities (within State) in India. It covers the years 2007-08 (Actual), 2008-09 (Actual), 2009-10 (Actual) and 2010-11 (Provisional), supporting analysis of energy loss trends and utility performance. The data is useful for planning, monitoring and policy evaluation by stakeholders focused on reducing losses and improving power sector efficiency under NITI Aayog.",
  "generated_sector": "Power and Energy; Non Renewable"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog brings together aggregate technical and commercial losses of State power utilities (SPUs) (within state) across India. It supports analysis of power sector performance by tracking loss levels over different years, enabling comparisons across states and time for planning, monitoring, and policy evaluation. The datasets are published by NITI Aayog and are useful for researchers, analysts, and program managers working on efficiency improvements and utility-level reforms in the power sector.",
  "generated_sector": "Power and Energy; Renewable"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog covers agriculture production, stock, and yield information for major crops and food grains across India. It tracks key indicators such as production volume, yield, and area under cultivation on both monthly and yearly bases, supporting analysis of crop performance over time. The datasets are useful for monitoring agricultural output trends, assessing productivity changes, and informing planning and policy decisions. Published under NITI Aayog, the focus is on crop-wise and foodgrain-wise achievements including oilseeds and cash/commercial crops.",
  "generated_sector": "Agriculture; Crops"
}

{
  "generated_description": "Agro-Ecological Zoning provides agro-ecological regions for India based on classifications by ICAR-NBSS&LUP, Nagpur. It supports planning and decision-making in agriculture by enabling region-wise assessment of land and production potential. The catalog is published by the Ministry of Agriculture and Farmers Welfare, Department of Agricultural Research and Education (DARE), and the Indian Council of Agricultural Research (ICAR), and is useful for research, extension, and development initiatives that require agro-ecological context.",
  "generated_sector": "Agriculture; Agricultural Research & Extension"
}

{
  "generated_description": "Air Pollution Concentration : Ujjain brings together information on air pollution levels for the City of Ujjain, Madhya Pradesh. The catalog supports monitoring and assessment of ambient air quality, helping urban stakeholders understand pollution concentration patterns and prioritize local mitigation actions. It is published under the Ministry of Housing and Urban Affairs through the Smart Cities Mission, with a focus on city-level environmental management.",
  "generated_sector": "Environment and Forest; Industrial Air Pollution"
}

{
  "generated_description": "Citywise air quality assessment for Sagar focuses on key ambient pollutants including PM2.5, PM10, NO2, O3 and SO2, using smart city and municipal/environmental monitoring inputs. The catalog supports understanding pollutant concentration patterns and pollution quality trends for urban air management and public health awareness. It is published under the Ministry of Housing and Urban Affairs as part of the Smart Cities Mission, with coverage for the City of Sagar, Madhya Pradesh.",
  "generated_sector": "Environment and Forest; Air Quality"
}

{
  "generated_description": "Monthly air quality monitoring data for Surat focuses on key pollutants including PM2.5, PM10, NO2, O3 and SO2. The catalog provides mean concentration levels that support tracking urban air pollution trends and assessing exposure to major particulate and gaseous contaminants. It is published under the Ministry of Housing and Urban Affairs through the Smart Cities Mission, with a city-level focus on Surat for urban planning, compliance and public awareness use cases.",
  "generated_sector": "Environment and Forest; Air Quality"
}

{
  "generated_description": "Air Quality S02, PM2.5, PM10, NO2, O3 : Udaipur provides city-level air quality monitoring focused on key pollutants including PM2.5, PM10, NO2, O3 and SO2. The catalog supports analysis of pollutant concentrations over time for urban air quality assessment and public health and environmental planning use cases. Data are sourced through meteorological and local monitoring arrangements such as Smart Cities sensors, with coordination involving the Ministry of Housing and Urban Affairs under the Smart Cities Mission. It covers the City of Udaipur, Rajasthan.",
  "generated_sector": "Environment and Forest; Air Quality"
}

{
  "generated_description": "Air Quality S02,PM2.5,PM10,NO2,O3 : Panaji provides monthly mean concentration data for key air pollutants—PM2.5, PM10, NO2, O3, and SO2—measured in Panaji, Goa. The catalog supports monitoring of urban air quality trends and can be used for smart city reporting, exposure assessment, and evaluating pollution patterns from sensor-based observations. It is published under the Ministry of Housing and Urban Affairs through the Smart Cities Mission, with a focus on Panaji.",
  "generated_sector": "Environment and Forest; Vehicular Air Pollution"
}

{
  "generated_description": "Monthly air quality monitoring data for Pune, Maharashtra, covering key pollutants including PM2.5, PM10, NO2, O3 and SO2. The catalog provides mean concentration levels derived from city sensor observations, supporting assessment of residential air pollution trends and exposure-related planning. It is published under the Ministry of Housing and Urban Affairs through the Smart Cities Mission, enabling local stakeholders to track changes over time and inform mitigation actions.",
  "generated_sector": "Environment and Forest; Residential Air Pollution"
}

{
  "generated_description": "Monthly air quality monitoring data for Saharanpur, Uttar Pradesh, covering key pollutants including PM2.5, PM10, NO2, O3 and SO2. The catalog provides mean concentration levels derived from city sensor observations, supporting assessment of urban air pollution trends and exposure-relevant indicators. It is published under the Ministry of Housing and Urban Affairs through the Smart Cities Mission, with use cases in local environmental management, public awareness, and planning for cleaner air in the city.",
  "generated_sector": "Environment and Forest; Vehicular Air Pollution"
}

{
  "generated_description": "Air Quality S02,PM2.5,PM10,NO2,O3 : Solapur brings together city-level measurements of key air pollutants—SO2, PM2.5, PM10, NO2 and O3—captured through smart city and monitoring sensor networks. The catalog supports tracking air quality trends and assessing exposure to residential air pollution in Solapur, Maharashtra. It is published under the Ministry of Housing and Urban Affairs through the Smart Cities Mission, with local participation from relevant state and municipal environment agencies.",
  "generated_sector": "Environment and Forest; Residential Air Pollution"
}

{
  "generated_description": "Monthly air quality monitoring data for Tumakuru, Karnataka, covering key pollutants including SO2, PM2.5, PM10, NO2 and O3. The catalog focuses on mean concentration levels derived from city air quality sensors, supporting assessment of residential air pollution and tracking changes over time for urban health and environmental planning. It is published under the Ministry of Housing and Urban Affairs through the Smart Cities Mission, with involvement from Karnataka and Tumakuru.",
  "generated_sector": "Environment and Forest; Residential Air Pollution"
}

{
  "generated_description": "Air Quality with respect to Respirable Suspended Particulate Matter (RSPM) in air quality stations under the National Air Quality Monitoring Programme (NAMP) provides annual average concentration data for RSPM across air quality monitoring stations in India. It supports comparison of observed levels with the National Ambient Air Quality Standards (NAAQS) and helps assess air pollution exposure in urban and rural settings. Published by the Ministry of Environment, Forest and Climate Change and the Central Pollution Control Board, the catalog is useful for environmental monitoring, compliance assessment, and public health-oriented analysis.",
  "generated_sector": "Environment and Forest; Industrial Air Pollution"
}

{
  "generated_description": "Air Quality with respect to Suspended Particulate Matter under National Air Quality Monitoring Programme (NAMP) compiles annual average SPM levels from air quality stations across India. It supports comparison of observed concentrations with National Ambient Air Quality Standards (NAAQS), enabling assessment of air pollution trends and compliance for urban and rural settings. Published by the Ministry of Environment, Forest and Climate Change and the Central Pollution Control Board, the catalog is useful for environmental monitoring, policy review, and targeted interventions addressing industrial, residential, and vehicular pollution sources.",
  "generated_sector": "Environment and Forest; Industrial Air Pollution, Environment and Forest; Residential Air Pollution, Environment and Forest; Vehicular Air Pollution"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog covers air traffic handled at all Indian airports, tracking aircraft movements, passenger traffic, and freight traffic during the year. It includes international and domestic components as well as totals, supporting analysis of aviation demand and airport throughput. The datasets are useful for monitoring trends in passenger and cargo flows, planning capacity, and assessing performance across India’s airport network. Published by the Ministry of Civil Aviation, the coverage spans aviation activity across India.",
  "generated_sector": "Transport; Aviation"
}

{
  "generated_description": "Air Traffic Statistics covers India’s air transport performance through operating and traffic indicators such as aircraft utilization, passengers carried, passenger kilometre performed, available seat kilometre, cargo carried, and tonne kilometre performed, along with passenger and weight load factors. It brings together monthly and annual/month-wise editions for the 2015-16 and 2016-17 periods, supporting trend analysis of capacity, utilization, and load across time. Published by the Ministry of Civil Aviation, the catalog is useful for monitoring aviation activity and planning capacity and operations.",
  "generated_sector": "Transport; Aviation"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog brings together state-wise air quality information for industrial areas monitored under the National Ambient Air Quality Monitoring Programme for a few states. It covers measurements from 2001 onwards, supporting analysis of pollution levels and trends in industrial settings. The datasets are useful for environmental monitoring, compliance assessment, and evidence-based planning by researchers and policymakers. Published under the Ministry of Statistics and Programme Implementation, the collection focuses on India-wide coverage across the participating states.",
  "generated_sector": "Environment and Forest; Ecology"
}

{
  "generated_description": "Air quality in residential areas under the National Ambient Air Quality Monitoring Programme, presented with India-wide coverage. The catalog compiles state-wise indicators that help track ambient air quality conditions specifically in residential settings, supporting monitoring, assessment, and policy review. Published by the Ministry of Statistics and Programme Implementation, the resources are useful for researchers, planners, and analysts studying environmental performance and trends across states.",
  "generated_sector": "Environment and Forest; Ecology"
}

{
  "generated_description": "AirSewa provides aviation-related information for India, covering flight schedules and status, along with airport services and frequently asked questions. The catalog supports quick access to operational and customer-facing details for travelers and aviation stakeholders. It is published by the Ministry of Civil Aviation and is useful for building travel assistance, service discovery, and FAQ-driven user experiences around airport and flight information.",
  "generated_sector": "Transport; Aviation"
